<x-layouts.site title="About" description="Why Horsefax exists: a permanent, evidence-backed record that follows a horse through its life.">
    <x-page-header eyebrow="About Horsefax" title="Every horse has a history. It should not be lost every time the horse changes hands." />
    <div class="wrap py-16 prose-hf max-w-[44em]">
        <p>Horses change barns, trainers and owners many times. Papers go missing, vet records stay in a clinic's files, show results sit in different associations' databases, and much of what people know about a horse lives in memory. When someone needs to know the horse, they get pieces.</p>
        <p>Horsefax keeps a lasting record of a horse's identity and history, with evidence and attribution, from foaling to retirement. It belongs with the horse, and its owner decides what is shared of what they add.</p>
        <h2>A database that grows every day</h2>
        <p>Horsefax is compiling the history that has already been made public: show results, pedigrees and auction results from associations, registries and sale companies, each kept with its source. Some horses already have extensive histories here; others have only a few records so far. Reports become more complete as we add sources and as owners and professionals contribute, and our goal is to work with registries, associations and the people who know the horses to build the most complete and reliable record we can.</p>
        <p>During our introductory launch, full records are free to anyone with a Horsefax account.</p>
        <h2>What we believe</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Evidence over claims.</strong> Every fact says how it is known.</li>
            <li><strong>Owners control what they add.</strong> Anything an owner or professional adds starts private; sharing is deliberate and can be revoked. History that was already published elsewhere is shown with its source.</li>
            <li><strong>No silent edits.</strong> Corrections add to the history rather than erase it, and every change is logged.</li>
            <li><strong>Honesty about gaps.</strong> A missing record is never treated as proof that nothing happened.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Horsefax is operated by {{ config('horsefax.operator') }}.</p>
    </div>
</x-layouts.site>
